\ Spitfire: the flying lesson, as if in a two-seater with an instructor in
\ the back seat, in a Mk I with the two-pitch propeller. The lesson is a
\ script of steps, each what the instructor says and a test of what the
\ pupil has done; the next step comes when the test passes, and not before
\ the instruction has been up for 6 seconds, so it can be read. The first
\ step starts the engine, the magnetos and then the starter; the last, after
\ the landing, stops it, the slow-running cut-out and then the magnetos off. The steps
\ follow the pilot's notes' use of the two-pitch propeller: started in
\ coarse, fine before the take-off, coarse after the safety speed with the
\ boost reduced, fine again for the landing; on the ground the tail-down
\ attitude, the throttle opened over seconds and the swing caught early on
\ the rudder before it becomes a ground loop, the tail raised by easing
\ the stick forward in the slipstream and checked with the nose just above
\ the horizon, the three-point landing and the brakes used in short presses so
\ she does not tip onto her nose; the right stick the torque
\ calls for as she leaves the ground at full power, about a quarter of the
\ stick in the flight model; their rudder trim, fully right
\ for the take-off (as the Spitfire II's Pilot's Notes set it), wound back
\ at cruise until the slip needle centres, and a little right again for the
\ approach with the power on; and their approach, 140 mph
\ with the wheels and flaps lowered, 85 mph on the final approach (as quoted
\ by historylearningsite.co.uk and a2asimulations.com's Spitfire I
\ reference section). Between
\ the take-off and the landing come the climb, cruise power, trim, turns,
\ and the stall and its recovery. The speeds the instructor gives for the
\ lift-off (90 mph) and the stall (80 mph clean) are the flight model's.
\ The Turnhouse line at the view's top right gives the field's bearing and
\ distance.

6 constant least-step-time

\ the aircraft's heading, its bank and its height
: heading-now ( -- degrees ) plane@attitude@forward heading-of ;
: bank-now ( -- degrees ) plane@attitude@right second asin negate 180 * PI / ;
: height-now ( -- metres ) plane@position second ;

\ how far a heading is from another, degrees either way
: heading-off ( heading wanted -- degrees ) - 540 + 360 mod 180 - abs ;

\ the indicated airspeed in miles an hour
: indicated-mph ( -- mph ) plane indicated-speed 2.23694 * ;

\ the distance to Turnhouse over the ground, metres
: home-distance ( -- metres )
	:target game@ plane@position v- spread to dz drop to dx
	dx sq dz sq + sqrt ;

\ the lesson's steps: what the instructor says, the test that ends the step, and for the trim a condition that must hold for 6 seconds
: lesson-steps ( -- steps )
	[ { :say "THIS IS YOUR INSTRUCTOR, IN THE BACK SEAT. WE'RE ON THE RUNWAY AT TURNHOUSE, WHEELS DOWN - THE GREEN LIGHT UNDER U/C, LEFT OF THE PANEL - AND FLAPS UP. SHE SITS TAIL-DOWN ON HER LITTLE TAILWHEEL, SO THE LONG NOSE HIDES THE RUNWAY AHEAD: WATCH ITS EDGES PAST EITHER SIDE OF THE NOSE. FIRST, START THE ENGINE: SWITCH ON THE MAGNETOS WITH M, THEN HOLD K FOR THE STARTER UNTIL SHE FIRES."
	    :done ( plane@running ) }
	  { :say "SHE'S RUNNING. THE PROPELLER IS IN COARSE PITCH, AS FOR WARMING UP. SELECT FINE PITCH FOR THE TAKE-OFF: W (LEFT STICK CLICK). THE PITCH LEVER BESIDE THE THROTTLE GOES FORWARD."
	    :done ( plane@fine ) }
	  { :say "FINE PITCH. AT FULL POWER THE PROPELLER'S TORQUE AND ITS SLIPSTREAM SWING HER TO THE LEFT, SO BEFORE WE OPEN UP, WIND THE RUDDER TRIM FULLY RIGHT: HOLD . (PERIOD, OR THE RIGHT SHOULDER). THE RUDDER WHEEL, BELOW THE PANEL ON THE LEFT, SHOWS IT."
	    :done ( plane@rudder-trim 0.95 >= plane@throttle 0.98 >= or ) }
	  { :say "RUDDER TRIM FULLY RIGHT: THE ENGINE CAN TURN FAST AND GIVE ITS FULL POWER. NOW OPEN THE THROTTLE SMOOTHLY ALL THE WAY OVER ABOUT FIVE SECONDS, NOT ALL AT ONCE: HOLD Q (D-PAD UP). THE BOOST GAUGE WITH THE RED RIM, RIGHT OF THE PANEL, COMES UP TO +6. THE MOMENT SHE ROLLS SHE STARTS TO SWING LEFT: CATCH IT AT ONCE WITH RIGHT RUDDER, X (LEFT STICK RIGHT)."
	    :done ( plane@throttle 0.98 >= ) }
	  { :say "KEEP HER STRAIGHT DOWN THE RUNWAY WITH THE RUDDER, Z AND X (THE LEFT STICK), SMALL AND EARLY: A SWING LEFT TO GROW TURNS INTO A GROUND LOOP THAT NO RUDDER CAN STOP. PAST 30 MPH EASE THE STICK FORWARD - THE UP ARROW (RIGHT STICK FORWARD) - AND THE SLIPSTREAM ON THE ELEVATOR LIFTS THE TAIL; SHE MAY SWING AS IT COMES UP, SO BE QUICK ON THE RUDDER. CHECK IT WITH THE NOSE JUST ABOVE THE HORIZON, THE STICK BACK TOWARD CENTRAL: HELD FORWARD, THE NOSE GOES ON DOWN AND THE PROPELLER STRIKES THE RUNWAY. TAIL UP, YOU CAN SEE AHEAD OVER THE NOSE. WHEN THE AIRSPEED PASSES 90 MPH, EASE THE STICK BACK - THE DOWN ARROW - AND SHE'LL LIFT OFF. THE MOMENT SHE LEAVES THE GROUND THE ENGINE'S TORQUE ROLLS HER LEFT, AND HARD AT THIS SLOW SPEED: BE READY WITH THE RIGHT ARROW (RIGHT STICK RIGHT), A QUARTER OF THE STICK, AND KEEP THE HORIZON BAR LEVEL."
	    :done ( plane@on-ground not height-now 20 > and ) }
	  { :say "WE'RE FLYING. HOLD THE WINGS LEVEL WITH A LITTLE RIGHT STICK: SMALL, STEADY PRESSES ON THE RIGHT ARROW, NOT BIG ONES, OR YOU'LL ROCK HER FROM SIDE TO SIDE. AS THE SPEED GROWS SHE NEEDS LESS. WHEELS UP NOW, BEFORE WE GATHER SPEED: G (Y). THE RED LIGHT SAYS THEY'RE UP."
	    :done ( plane@gear not ) }
	  { :say "PAST THE SAFETY SPEED, THROTTLE BACK A LITTLE FROM FULL WITH A (D-PAD DOWN), THEN SELECT COARSE PITCH: S (LEFT STICK CLICK). IN FINE PITCH SHE'D OVER-REV AS THE SPEED GROWS; THE REVOLUTION COUNTER, RIGHT OF THE PANEL, DROPS."
	    :done ( plane@fine not plane@throttle 0.95 < and ) }
	  { :say "CLIMB AWAY AT ABOUT 160 MPH: IF THE SPEED FALLS, LOWER THE NOSE; IF IT RISES, RAISE IT. TAKE HER UP TO 3,000 FEET - THE ALTIMETER'S LONG HAND GOES ROUND ONCE EVERY THOUSAND FEET, THE SHORT ONE COUNTS THE THOUSANDS."
	    :done ( height-now 914 > ) }
	  { :say "LEVEL OFF AT 3,000, AND SET CRUISE POWER: THROTTLE BACK TO ABOUT +2 BOOST. LESS NOISE, LESS FUEL, LESS HEAT - KEEP AN EYE ON THE RAD AND OIL TEMPERATURES, BOTTOM RIGHT."
	    :done ( plane@boost 3 <= plane@velocity second abs 3 < and ) }
	  { :say "AS THE SPEED SETTLES SHE'LL WANT TO CLIMB OR SINK. TRIM IT OUT: ] WINDS IN NOSE-UP, [ NOSE-DOWN (LEFT STICK BACK AND FORWARD); THE TRIM INDICATOR, LEFT OF THE PANEL, SHOWS WHERE IT IS. TRIM UNTIL SHE HOLDS HER HEIGHT WITH YOUR HANDS OFF THE STICK, THE CLIMB NEEDLE STEADY ON ITS ZERO."
	    :done ( :hold-time game@ 6 >= ) :hold ( controls :pitch-free false @or plane@velocity second abs 1.5 < and ) }
	  { :say "NOW THE RUDDER TRIM. IT'S STILL FULLY RIGHT FROM THE TAKE-OFF, BUT AT CRUISE POWER THE ENGINE HARDLY SWINGS HER, SO THE TRIM PUSHES THE NOSE RIGHT AND SHE SLIPS: THE SLIP NEEDLE, TOP OF THE TURN AND SLIP INDICATOR, BOTTOM RIGHT OF THE BLIND-FLYING PANEL, SITS OFF CENTRE. WIND IT BACK WITH , (COMMA, OR THE LEFT SHOULDER) UNTIL THE NEEDLE CENTRES WITH YOUR FEET OFF THE PEDALS."
	    :done ( :hold-time game@ 6 >= ) :hold ( controls :yaw-free false @or plane air-velocity plane@attitude@right v-dot abs 2 < and ) }
	  { :say "NICELY TRIMMED. NOW A TURN. ROLL LEFT WITH THE LEFT ARROW TO ABOUT 30 DEGREES OF BANK - THE HORIZON BAR TILTS WITH YOU - THEN HOLD A LITTLE BACK STICK SO THE NOSE DOESN'T DROP. TURN UNTIL THE GYRO READS 240, AND ROLL LEVEL."
	    :done ( heading-now 240 heading-off 10 < bank-now abs 10 < and ) }
	  { :say "GOOD. NOW TURN RIGHT, ONTO 060, THE SAME WAY. KEEP YOUR HEIGHT: WATCH THE ALTIMETER AS WELL AS THE GYRO."
	    :done ( heading-now 60 heading-off 10 < bank-now abs 10 < and ) }
	  { :say "NOW THE STALL, SO YOU KNOW IT WHEN IT COMES. CLOSE THE THROTTLE (A) AND KEEP THE NOSE UP WITH BACK STICK AS SHE SLOWS. AT ABOUT 80 MPH THE WING STOPS LIFTING AND THE NOSE DROPS: THAT'S THE STALL."
	    :done ( plane@angle-of-attack plane@type@stall-angle > ) }
	  { :say "SHE'S STALLED. RECOVER: STICK FORWARD TO GET THE AIR FLOWING OVER THE WING AGAIN, THEN THROTTLE OPEN (Q), AND EASE HER OUT OF THE DIVE. DON'T PULL TOO HARD, OR SHE'LL STALL AGAIN."
	    :done ( indicated-mph 150 > plane@velocity second -2 > and ) }
	  { :say "WELL RECOVERED. NOW HOME TO LAND. THE TURNHOUSE LINE AT THE TOP RIGHT OF THE VIEW GIVES THE FIELD'S BEARING AND DISTANCE: TURN ONTO THAT BEARING ON THE GYRO, THROTTLE BACK, AND COME DOWN TO 1,000 FEET AS WE GO."
	    :done ( home-distance 8000 < height-now 400 < and ) }
	  { :say "THROTTLE BACK AND SLOW TO 140 MPH. THEN THE DRILL BEFORE LANDING: UNDERCARRIAGE DOWN, G (Y), AND LOOK FOR THE GREEN LIGHT; PROPELLER TO FINE PITCH, W, SO THE FULL POWER IS THERE IF WE HAVE TO GO ROUND."
	    :done ( plane@gear plane@fine and ) }
	  { :say "NOW FLAPS DOWN: F (X). NEVER ABOVE 140 MPH - THE PLATE ON THE LEFT SAYS SO, AND THE AIR WOULD BLOW THEM BACK UP. THE NOSE DROPS AS THEY COME DOWN: WIND ON NOSE-UP TRIM WITH ] TO HOLD IT."
	    :done ( plane@flap-setting 0.9 > ) }
	  { :say "THE RUNWAY RUNS 060 AND 240. LINE UP WITH IT AND COME DOWN STEADILY, SLOWING TO 85 MPH ON THE FINAL APPROACH, THE NOSE A LITTLE HIGH: THE THROTTLE FOR THE SPEED, THE STICK FOR THE DESCENT. WITH THE POWER ON AND THE WHEELS AND FLAPS DOWN SHE SWINGS LEFT: A LITTLE RIGHT RUDDER TRIM, ., UNTIL THE SLIP NEEDLE CENTRES. OVER THE END OF THE RUNWAY CLOSE THE THROTTLE AND KEEP BRINGING THE STICK BACK, HOLDING HER OFF, SO SHE SETTLES TAIL-DOWN ON ALL THREE WHEELS TOGETHER."
	    :done ( plane@on-ground ) }
	  { :say "WE'RE DOWN. STICK FULLY BACK TO HOLD THE TAIL DOWN, AND KEEP HER STRAIGHT WITH THE RUDDER: SHE CAN STILL SWING. BRAKE IN SHORT PRESSES OF B (B), NOT HELD: HELD, THE BRAKES TIP HER ONTO HER NOSE AND PUT THE PROPELLER INTO THE GROUND. THE RUDDER BAR SHARES THE BRAKING BETWEEN THE WHEELS, SO RUDDER WITH THE BRAKE STEERS HER. FLAPS UP ONCE WE'RE STOPPED."
	    :done ( plane@velocity v-length 3 < ) }
	  { :say "NOW STOP THE ENGINE: HOLD O, THE SLOW-RUNNING CUT-OUT, UNTIL SHE STOPS; THEN MAGNETOS OFF WITH M."
	    :done ( plane@running not plane@magnetos not and ) }
	  { :say "THAT'S THE LESSON. WELL FLOWN. ESCAPE FOR THE MISSIONS."
	    :done ( false ) } ] ;

\ a lesson's step, of the steps given: its time runs, and while the step's hold holds, its hold time; once the instruction has been up its least time and the test passes, the next step and its instruction, shown until that step ends
: run-lesson ( steps dt -- )
	| steps dt |
	plane@crashed if exit then
	steps :lesson-step game@ @i to step
	:step-time game@ dt + :step-time game!
	step :hold null @or to hold
	hold null? not if
		hold execute if :hold-time game@ dt + else 0 then :hold-time game!
	then
	:step-time game@ least-step-time < if exit then
	step@done execute not if exit then
	:lesson-step game@ 1+ steps size 1- min2 :lesson-step game!
	0 :step-time game!
	0 :hold-time game!
	steps :lesson-step game@ @i to next-step
	next-step@say to instruction
	instruction :instruction game!
	next-step :brief null @or :brief game!
	instruction reading-pause ;

\ the lesson's lines at the view's top right: the step, and Turnhouse's bearing and distance over the ground
: draw-lesson-panel ( -- )
	lesson-steps size :lesson-step game@ 1+ "LESSON, STEP {0} OF {1}" format to step-line
	step-line 0 0xffe080 info-line
	:target game@ plane@position v- spread to dz drop to dx
	home-distance 1609.34 / [ dx 0 dz ] heading-of "TURNHOUSE {0:03.0f} {1:.1f} MI" format to target-line
	target-line 1 dial-ink info-line ;
